- op: discuss  # 9711
  at: '2026-06-02T03:24:04Z'  # 9711
  by: agent  # 9711
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9711
  clock: 6  # 9711
  nonce: '9711'  # 9711
  message: "Pass-21 confirmation observation. Re-measured field population on fresh post-INV-sugat-closure substrate (`/tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json`, 84 AnalysisRuns):\n\n- AR.failed_files: 0/84 (0%) populated\n- AR.warnings: 0/84 (0%) populated  \n- AR.skipped_passes: 0/84 (0%) populated\n\nThe three 'reserved provenance fields' identified by this invariant remain 100% empty across all AnalysisRuns. Either (a) the fix was not actually deployed and INV-virik should flip pending_validation → violated, or (b) these fields are correctly empty when there are no failures/warnings/skips and the invariant title overclaims. Suggesting (a) given that we'd expect SOME warnings across 84 passes on a 902-file codebase — `warnings: []` for every single AnalysisRun is suspicious. Pass-21 notebook entry: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06012026_2310_pass21.md`."  # 9711
- op: discuss  # 463a
  at: '2026-06-02T03:37:06Z'  # 463a
  by: agent  # 463a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 463a
  clock: 7  # 463a
  nonce: 463a  # 463a
  message: "Pass-22 sub-finding (F10) — the reserved-empty pattern extends to top-level `limits` (not just per-AnalysisRun records).\n\nPass-22 substrate shows the following always-empty lists at top level:\n- `limits.failed_files: []`\n- `limits.skipped_languages: []`\n- `limits.truncated_files: []`\n- `limits.supply_chain.ambiguous_paths: []`\n- `limits.supply_chain.classification_failures: []`\n\nSame INV-virik pattern (schema reserves the field, writer never populates), different surface. The top-level `limits` section is supposed to carry global rollups of per-AR failures/skips/truncations; the per-AR records also have these empty (the pass-21 INV-virik observation). Both layers leak.\n\nEither: widen INV-virik's title to cover both layers, or file a sibling for the top-level case. The fix is the same — populate the field when there are actual entries, and add a writer-contract validator entry that requires consistency between top-level rollup and per-AR sums.\n\nLab notebook entry: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06012026_2340_pass22.md`."  # 463a
- op: discuss  # 448d
  at: '2026-06-02T04:38:23Z'  # 448d
  by: agent  # 448d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 448d
  clock: 8  # 448d
  nonce: 448d  # 448d
  message: "**Pass-23 finding (F23.7) — kind-conditioned silent population of node.shape_id and node.fingerprint.**\n\n| node.kind | Total | shape_id NULL | fingerprint NULL |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| method | 18,290 | 0.01% | **21.38%** |\n| function | 7,098 | 2.01% | 1.83% |\n| class | 4,444 | 0.02% | 0.00% |\n| variable | 1,609 | **99.94%** | 0.19% |\n| external_symbol | 1,638 | 100% (intentional) | 100% (intentional) |\n| file | 901 | 100% (intentional) | 0.11% |\n| call_site | 130 | 100% (intentional) | 100% (intentional) |\n| dependency | 82 | 100% (intentional) | 0.00% |\n| interface | 7 | 28.57% | 0.00% |\n\nThe 100% NULL pattern on `external_symbol`/`call_site`/`dependency` is intentional (these are references, not declarations). Surprises:\n\n- `variable`: 99.94% NULL on shape_id — 1,608 of 1,609 variables lack shape_id. Variables ARE declarations (they have AST positions, a value expression, etc.) so the absence isn't structurally forced. One variable has a shape_id — likely a corner case worth investigating, but the pattern says \"writer applies shape_id only to callable kinds.\"\n- `method`: 21.38% NULL on fingerprint — 3,911 of 18,290 methods lack a fingerprint, despite class (0.00%) and function (1.83%) being well below 5%. The methods missing fingerprint are likely synthetic stand-ins or methods on synthetic classes (class is at 0.00% NULL but contains some of those).\n\n**Significance.** Same INV-virik sub-pattern (1) \"schema declares, no writer wires\" — but kind-conditioned. The schema documents `shape_id` and `fingerprint` as universal Node fields. The writer applies them only conditionally on kind, but the condition isn't declared in the dataclass or spec.\n\n**Suggested action.** Either (a) split the dataclass so shape_id and fingerprint live on a `ShapeBearing` mixin that the kinds-with-shape opt into (parallel to the ADR-0032 typed-sibling pattern for display_label), or (b) declare the kind-conditioning explicitly: `# shape_id is populated for function/method/class; NULL for leaf kinds. See ADR-XXXX`. Solution (a) is structural and would prevent silent-partial-population at the type level; solution (b) is documentation-only.\n\n**Cluster.** Falls under INV-virik (P1 pending_validation, parent INV-luhur) as a per-Node face complementing the per-AnalysisRun faces already filed. The variable shape_id and method fingerprint gaps are sub-faces. Could also fold into INV-jusot's modifier-vocabulary direction as \"kind-conditioned schema-field partial population is a broader axis we should declare explicitly.\" For now, this discussion entry is the record.\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_0010_pass23.md`."  # 448d
- op: discuss  # c597
  at: '2026-06-02T04:53:23Z'  # c597
  by: agent  # c597
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c597
  clock: 9  # c597
  nonce: c597  # c597
  message: "**Pass-24 substrate-verified faces (F24.2, F24.5) on reserved-empty patterns + entrypoint provenance.**\n\n**(F24.2) `limits.partial_results_reason = ''` (empty string, not None).** Of the 10 fields in `limits.*` on pass-21+ substrate:\n- 5 fields are `[]` (list-typed reserved-empty): `failed_files`, `skipped_languages`, `truncated_files`, `supply_chain.ambiguous_paths`, `supply_chain.classification_failures`.\n- 1 field is `''` (string-typed reserved-empty): `partial_results_reason`.\n\nINV-virik covers the `[]` family at the AR layer and (per pass-22 F10) the same pattern at top-level limits. Pass-24 surfaces the string-typed variant: three different empty conventions in the same top-level dict. A consumer asking \"did the run hit partial-results conditions?\" gets `''` which is falsy in most parsers — they'd correctly conclude \"no partial results.\" But if a producer sets it to a meaningful string later, downstream consumer code must change from `if reason:` to `if reason and reason != ''` — a subtle bug surface. Either always omit unpopulated fields, or have the schema declare the empty-value convention per field type.\n\n**(F24.5) Entrypoint records lack `evidence_type` / `source` provenance.** All 104 entrypoint records carry exactly 4 fields: `confidence, kind, label, symbol_id`. No `evidence_type`, no `source`, no `derivation_method`.\n\n```\nsample (kind=library_export):\n  confidence: 0.675\n  kind: library_export\n  label: \"Library export: TrackerSet\"\n  symbol_id: python:.../trackerset.py:87-997:TrackerSet:class\n```\n\nEdge records carry both `meta.evidence_type` (33 distinct values) AND `confidence`, so consumers can interpret e.g. `confidence=0.85 from evidence_type=ast_call_direct` differently than `confidence=0.85 from evidence_type=naming_convention`. Entrypoint records carry confidence without that anchor.\n\nPass-22 F8 (INV-suvil) surfaced that library_export confidence is non-round computed (0.18-0.67, 34 distinct values across 46 entries) but the consumer can't tell whether 0.184 means \"low signal name match\" or \"weak heuristic export inference.\" F24.5 surfaces the WHY-can't-we-tell: provenance fields absent from the schema.\n\nEither schema-extend entrypoint records with `evidence_type` + `source` (mirror edge.meta), or add a separate `entrypoint_provenance` section. The fix shape is sub-pattern (1) of INV-luhur \"schema declares no writer wires\" — except here it's \"schema doesn't declare at all.\"\n\nBoth faces are discussion-only; no new tracker items.\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_0250_pass24.md`."  # c597
- op: discuss  # cd34
  at: '2026-06-02T05:21:47Z'  # cd34
  by: agent  # cd34
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cd34
  clock: 10  # cd34
  nonce: cd34  # cd34
  message: "Pass-25 cross-format consistency probe — origin field family has THREE parallel encodings of \"where did this node come from\" with inconsistent emptiness sentinels:\n\nF25.4: `node.origin_run_id` carries `''` (empty string) on 2228 nodes (6.50%) — 1638 external_symbol + 492 file + 82 dependency + 7 project + 9 other kinds. Languages: python 1992, markdown 106, toml 83, typescript 19, json 8, wgsl 5, rust 4, go 3, sql 3, swift 2, javascript 1, java 1, solidity 1. Empty-string-typed reserved-empty, same anti-pattern as F24.2 (`limits.partial_results_reason=''`). Recommendation: emit `None` (omit the field) instead of `''` to match the type contract of \"FK that points at no AR.\"\n\nF25.6: `node.origin_run_pass_id` is None on 100% of all 34253 nodes — both populated-origin_run_id and empty-origin_run_id cases. Schema field exists, no writer populates it. Pure reserved-empty extending INV-virik's existing scope. (Direct addition to the catalog of fields declared in the schema but never written.)\n\nCompanion sub-finding (overlaps INV-numat): the same record has `origin` field (list, always length 1) carrying values like ['python'], ['orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis'], ['toml'], or `[]` for external_symbol. THREE fields encoding origin info with inconsistent emptiness: when origin_run_id is empty, origin is sometimes `[]` (1638 external_symbol cases) and sometimes `['orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis']` (491 file/project cases) and sometimes `['toml']`/`['json']`/`['wgsl']` (95 cases). origin_run_pass_id is None across all three subcases. List-of-1 + inconsistent-empty-sentinel + 100%-null-companion-field is a multi-axis reserved-empty pattern.\n\nPass-24 F24.2 (`partial_results_reason=''`) and pass-25 F25.4 are concrete data points for INV-virik's \"string-typed reserved-empty\" face; F25.6 is the cleaner \"schema-declared field never written\" face. The list-of-1 / inconsistent sentinels portion is mainly an INV-numat concern (axis-mixing on the origin family) and is referenced there."  # cd34
- op: discuss  # 4f2a
  at: '2026-06-02T05:47:41Z'  # 4f2a
  by: agent  # 4f2a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4f2a
  clock: 11  # 4f2a
  nonce: 4f2a  # 4f2a
  message: "Pass-26 provenance-chain probes — three more reserved-empty / missing-field instances:\n\nF26.9: `bm.repo_fingerprint` is **None** at the top-level of bm.json, while `bm.repo_fingerprint_scheme` is populated (\"hypergumbo-repofp-v1\"). The scheme declaration implies the field exists in the schema. All 84 AR.repo_fingerprint values are identical (uniform `01531b2e29...`); the same fingerprint should be lifted to the bm-level field. Three options: (a) populate bm.repo_fingerprint from AR.repo_fingerprint (since they're uniform); (b) drop bm.repo_fingerprint from schema if AR-level is canonical; (c) document that bm.repo_fingerprint is intentionally absent (e.g., \"use ARs[0].repo_fingerprint\"). Status quo confuses consumers reading the top-level field.\n\nF26.10: 108 nodes have **both** `stable_id=None` AND `language=None` — these are 100% linker-emitted synthetic kinds (function 32 / class 7 / struct 5 / enum 5 / call_site 78 / etc.). The cohort overlap is structural: nodes whose canonical-input is incomplete fail both stable_id derivation (per ADR-0034 ID-construction discipline) and language attribution. Total stable_id=None = 136; total language=None = 262; intersection = 108. So stable_id=None has 28 cases with language populated (28 ≈ typescript class nodes from htrac-frontend whose typescript-class declarations lack stable_id), and language=None has 154 cases with stable_id populated (the synthetic linker function/call_site cohort from F26.1).\n\n(P17 correction over pass-25: pass-25 finding F25.5 reported \"stable_id='' empty string\" cohort — that was a probe-bucketing artifact. Actual: stable_id=None on 136 nodes; stable_id='' on 0 nodes. The 'empty' category in pass-25's regex bucket conflated None and '' via `.get('stable_id', '') or ''`.)\n\nF26.14: `AR.warnings=[]` (empty list) on **all 84 ARs**. The field is declared in the AR dataclass (ir.py:200, `warnings: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)`) and serialized in every record. No AR ever writes anything to it. Pure reserved-empty extending the catalog already containing pass_version='' (14 ARs), partial_results_reason='' (top-level), origin_run_id='' (2228 nodes), failed_files=[] (limits + AR), etc.\n\nThe cumulative reserved-empty inventory across passes 23-26 (pass-23 F23.7, pass-24 F24.2, pass-25 F25.4/F25.6, pass-26 F26.9/F26.10/F26.14) is now ~10 distinct schema fields that are declared-and-serialized but never written. The \"schema field exists / writer never populates\" pattern that INV-virik umbrellas continues to surface at new fields each pass; the structural fix isn't piecewise — it's the kind-conditional / reason-conditional schema marking already discussed in WI-bujot's pass-25 thread."  # 4f2a
- op: discuss  # 3467
  at: '2026-06-02T06:13:59Z'  # 3467
  by: agent  # 3467
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3467
  clock: 12  # 3467
  nonce: '3467'  # 3467
  message: "Pass-27 INV-virik — three additional reserved-empty / kind-conditioned faces.\n\nPass-26 F26.9 + F26.10 + F26.14 added the reserved-empty cohort at bm.repo_fingerprint=None top-level + 108 nodes with stable_id=None + AR.warnings=[] across all 84 ARs. Pass-27 adds three more:\n\n**F27.6: `bm.fingerprint_scheme = None` top-level.** Schema declares the field (parallel to stable_id_scheme='hypergumbo-stableid-v5' and shape_id_scheme='hypergumbo-shapeid-v2' which ARE populated). Producer writes None. Same family as F26.9 (bm.repo_fingerprint=None). Schema declares three scheme-name fields; two populate, one doesn't. Pattern: the third top-level scheme field is the inconsistent one.\n\n**F27.7: `bm.toolchain = {}` empty-dict top-level.** Per-AR `toolchain` is populated with detailed runtime info (`{name, version, grammar_module}`); the top-level bm.toolchain is `{}`. Same reserved-empty shape as F26.9, but with dict-typed sentinel. Extends the reserved-empty catalog to include dict-typed reserved-empty (prior catalog: None, '', [] / now adds {}).\n\n**F27.10: `Symbol.stable_id` 100% NULL on synthetic-kind nodes.** Kind-conditioned writer pattern (pass-23 F23.7 / pass-25 F25.7 sub-pattern 3) applied to stable_id specifically:\n\n```\nkind        | total | stable_id=None | %\nmethod      | 18290 |       1 |   0.0%\nfunction    |  7098 |      32 |   0.5%\nclass       |  4444 |       7 |   0.2%\npackage     |     3 |       1 |  33.3%\ncall_site   |   130 |      78 |  60.0%\nenum        |     5 |       5 | 100.0%\nstruct      |     5 |       5 | 100.0%\ntrait       |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\nprotocol    |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\ncontract    |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\nevent       |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\nconstructor |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\nmodifier    |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\nalias       |     1 |       1 | 100.0%\n```\n\nThe 8 exotic kinds (enum/struct/trait/protocol/contract/event/constructor/modifier/alias) have 100% stable_id NULL. These are all linker-emitted synthetic kinds. The stable_id writer never populates them. call_site is at 60% NULL (78/130) for the linker-synth subset.\n\nCombined with pass-26 F26.10 (108 nodes have BOTH stable_id=None AND language=None — also the linker-synth cohort), the structural picture is: synthetic-kind writers DON'T fill in the ADR-required fields. The validator's writer-contract class catches per-AR fields but per-Node-kind gaps slip through. Cumulative cohort: 136 stable_id=None nodes total = 108 (F26.10 stable_id+language NULL) + 28 more spread across the kind table.\n\nCumulative reserved-empty catalog across passes 24/25/26/27 — now ~13 distinct fields/cohorts:\n- Reserved-empty top-level scheme: bm.repo_fingerprint=None (F26.9), bm.fingerprint_scheme=None (F27.6)\n- Reserved-empty top-level dict: bm.toolchain={} (F27.7)\n- Reserved-empty AR field: AR.warnings=[] all 84 (F26.14)\n- Reserved-empty Node field — kind-conditioned: stable_id=None on 8 exotic synthetic kinds + 60% of call_site (F27.10); origin_run_pass_id=None all 34253 (F25.6); origin_run_id='' on 2228 string-typed (F25.4)\n- Reserved-empty Node nested: node.quality=None (existing)\n- Reserved-empty AR.pass_version='' on 14 (F26.13 / WI-mipul scope)\n- Reserved-empty limits: failed_files=[] / skipped_languages=[] / truncated_files=[] / partial_results_reason='' (F22 / F24.2)\n- Reserved-empty edge: edge.provenance={} all 109915 (existing)\n\nProbe artifact: /tmp/pass27_probe2.py + /tmp/pass27_probe5.py + /tmp/pass27_probe6.py / outputs at /tmp/pass27_output[2,5,6].log.\n\nNo status change; pass-27 enriches reserved-empty + kind-conditioned-writer catalogs."  # 3467
