  clock: 13  # 37fc
  nonce: 37fc  # 37fc
  message: "Pass-28 INV-virik — two additional reserved-empty / kind-conditioned-writer faces.\n\n**F28.2: edge.evidence_lang + edge.evidence_spans dataclass-declared but ABSENT from substrate.**\n\nir.py Edge dataclass declares:\n- `evidence_lang: Optional[str] = None` (line 611)\n- `evidence_spans: Optional[List[Dict[str, Any]]] = None` (line 612)\n\nSpec.md line 799 documents:\n> The top-level `meta.evidence_type`, `meta.evidence_lang`, and `meta.evidence_spans` always reflect the primary (highest-confidence) record.\n\nBut `Edge.to_dict()` (ir.py:728-734) writes these CONDITIONALLY:\n```python\nmeta: Dict[str, Any] = {\"evidence_type\": self.evidence_type}\nif self.evidence_lang is not None:\n    meta[\"evidence_lang\"] = self.evidence_lang\nif self.evidence_spans is not None:\n    meta[\"evidence_spans\"] = self.evidence_spans\n```\n\nSubstrate verification: 0 of 109,915 edges has `evidence_lang` in meta; 0 has `evidence_spans`. Every producer leaves both at the dataclass default (None), and the conditional writer skips the key entirely. Two ir.py-declared + spec.md-documented fields are 100% absent from the substrate.\n\nReserved-empty pattern face: declared-and-documented + writer-suppresses-default → field never appears. Cousin of F26.14 (AR.warnings=[] all 84) and F25.6 (origin_run_pass_id=None all 34253), but with a NEW sentinel-mechanism: the conditional write means absence-rather-than-None on the wire.\n\n**F28.5: Kind-conditioned-writer pattern applies at scale to FIVE introspection fields (not just stable_id).**\n\nPass-23 F23.7 found fingerprint 21% NULL on method-kind; pass-25 F25.7 catalogued is_exported / qualified_name / signature by kind; pass-27 F27.10 catalogued stable_id by kind. Pass-28 generalizes: the kind-conditioned-writer pattern applies broadly across at least 5 introspection fields. Table from /tmp/pass28_probe4.py Q1:\n\n```\nkind        | count | fingerprint% | shape_id% | qualified% | doc% | sig%\nmethod      | 18290 |       21.4%  |     0.0%  |    99.9%   | 25.3%|  0.0%\nfunction    |  7098 |        1.8%  |     2.0%  |    99.8%   | 20.8%|  1.9%\nclass       |  4444 |        0.0%  |     0.0%  |    99.8%   | 10.3%|100.0%\nexternal_symbol | 1638 |    100.0%  |   100.0%  |   100.0%   |100.0%|100.0%\nvariable    |  1609 |        0.2%  |    99.9%  |   100.0%   |100.0%|100.0%\nfile        |   901 |        0.1%  |   100.0%  |   100.0%   |100.0%|100.0%\ncall_site   |   130 |      100.0%  |   100.0%  |   100.0%   |100.0%|100.0%\ndependency  |    82 |        0.0%  |   100.0%  |   100.0%   |100.0%|100.0%\nexport      |    20 |        0.0%  |     0.0%  |   100.0%   | 85.0%|100.0%\n```\n\nPattern:\n- **method/function/class** (the 30k \"real\" Python symbols) are well-populated on fingerprint/shape_id, partially on docstring/signature, near-zero on qualified_name (WI-fagab residual).\n- **external_symbol / call_site** (linker-synth) are 100% NULL on every introspection field.\n- **variable / file / dependency** are 100% NULL on shape_id + sig + doc + qualified_name (these kinds don't have those concepts — design-intentional).\n- **class.signature = 100% NULL** confirmed (class has no signature concept).\n\nThe pattern across passes 23/25/27/28 is now structurally clear: the introspection-field writers are correctly conditional on (kind, field) — but the schema declares the fields universally without marking which (kind, field) pairs the writer is REQUIRED to populate. The validator's writer-contract class catches per-AR field gaps; per-(kind,field) gaps slip through.\n\nRecommended fix path candidate: ir.py per-field docstring should add a kind-applicability matrix, OR a writer-contract per-(kind,field) check class added to the validator stage.\n\nReserved-empty / declared-but-conditional cumulative catalog now ~15 distinct fields/cohorts across passes 24-28.\n\nProbe artifact: /tmp/pass28_probe2.py (evidence_lang/spans absence verification) + /tmp/pass28_probe4.py (kind-conditioned table) / outputs at /tmp/pass28_output[2,4].log."  # 37fc
- op: discuss  # 7ccb
  at: '2026-06-02T06:40:39Z'  # 7ccb
  by: agent  # 7ccb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7ccb
  clock: 14  # 7ccb
  nonce: 7ccb  # 7ccb
  message: "Pass-29 INV-virik — complete per-(kind, field) NULL matrix for kind-conditioned writer pattern (26 kinds × 12 introspection fields = 312 cells).\n\nPass-23 F23.7 / pass-27 F27.10 / pass-28 F28.4 progressively widened the kind-conditioned-writer observation. Pass-29 produces the complete enumeration. Of 312 (kind, field) cells, **194 (62.2%) are 100%-NULL** on the substrate. Of those 194, only **7 have a documented design rationale** (e.g., class has no signature, file has no docstring). The remaining 187 cells require a spec consult to classify \"writer-contract gap\" vs \"design-correct\".\n\n**Full matrix** (NULL rate %, 100% = entire kind's nodes have that field NULL; truncated to most-populated 8 kinds):\n\n```\nkind              | count|stable_|shape_i|fingerp|qualifi|docstri|signatu|cycloma|lines_o|display|discove|protoco|modifie\nmethod            | 18290|   0.0%|   0.0%|  21.4%|  99.9%|  25.3%|   0.0%|   0.0%|   0.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|  97.7%\nfunction          |  7098|   0.5%|   2.0%|   1.8%|  99.8%|  20.8%|   1.9%|   4.2%|   2.0%| 100.0%|  98.2%|  98.2%|  60.7%\nclass             |  4444|   0.2%|   0.0%|   0.0%|  99.8%|  10.3%| 100.0%|   0.2%|   0.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|  98.3%\nexternal_symbol   |  1638|   0.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|   0.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%\nvariable          |  1609|   0.0%|  99.9%|   0.2%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|  99.9%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|  51.7%\nfile              |   901|   0.0%| 100.0%|   0.1%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|  99.0%|  99.9%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%\ncall_site         |   130|  60.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%|   0.0%|   0.0%| 100.0%\ndependency        |    82|   0.0%| 100.0%|   0.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%\nexport            |    20|   0.0%|   0.0%|   0.0%| 100.0%|  85.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%| 100.0%\n```\n\n(Tail: 16 more low-count kinds — interface 7, project 7, enum 5, struct 5, package 3, getter 2, type 2, trait/protocol/contract/event/constructor/modifier/alias/view/index/table 1 each — all show similar 100%-NULL profiles on most fields.)\n\n**Cell verdict summary** (manual classification + 'UNCLASSIFIED' default):\n\n| Verdict | Count | Sample cells |\n|---|---:|---|\n| design-correct (kind doesn't have field concept) | 7 | (class, signature) — classes have no signature; (file, docstring) — files have no docstring concept; (variable, signature/docstring) — variables have no signatures; (external_symbol, fingerprint/docstring) — pure references; (call_site, fingerprint) — synthetic |\n| UNCLASSIFIED — needs spec consult | 187 | All (rare_kind, common_field) pairs where spec doesn't say whether the field is expected on that kind |\n\nThe **187 unclassified cells** are the kind-conditioned-writer pattern at its full scope. For each, the spec either (a) names the field as part of the universal Symbol schema (suggesting writer-contract gap if NULL) or (b) doesn't mention it (suggesting design-may-be-correct).\n\n**Concrete writer-contract candidates** (where method/function/class have well-populated values BUT a synthetic-or-edge kind doesn't):\n- `(external_symbol, modifiers)` — modifiers is a List[str]; absent or empty across all 1638 external_symbols. May be design-correct (external references have no observed modifiers).\n- `(method/function/class, display_label)` — display_label is ADR-0032 Class B reserved-only (per META-huvuh); the 100% NULL on method/function/class IS the contrapositive that the validator enforces. NOT a writer-contract gap; consistent with the cross_field invariant.\n- `(method/function/class, discovery_language)` — discovery_language is ADR-0031 Class B reserved-only (synthetic stand-ins); the 100% NULL on real source kinds is the contrapositive (mutually exclusive with `language`). NOT a writer-contract gap.\n- `(call_site, discovery_language) = 0% NULL` — i.e., 100% populated! call_site is a synthetic kind (linker emission) that DOES set discovery_language. Same for protocol_origin (0% NULL on call_site).\n\n**Implications:**\n- The matrix surfaces 187 cells that need spec.md to be CONSULTED, but spec doesn't carry a per-(kind, field) applicability declaration anywhere.\n- F28.4 fix-path candidate (kind-applicability matrix in ir.py docstrings OR per-(kind, field) validator class) is substantiated: the validator-class addition would need to encode 187+ rules to fully gate the contrastive cases.\n- Some cells ARE correctly classified by existing validator logic (e.g., display_label / discovery_language Class B contrapositives) — those should be excluded from the new writer-contract scope.\n- The biggest residual writer-contract gaps are likely:\n  - `(method, fingerprint) = 21.4% NULL` — pass-23 F23.7 covered.\n  - `(call_site, stable_id) = 60.0% NULL` — F27.10 covered.\n  - All `(synthetic_kind, stable_id) = 100% NULL` — F27.10 / F28.4 covered.\n\nThe 187 unclassified cells primarily reflect \"rare-kind has 1-5 nodes, all NULL on most fields\" — investigating each is low-yield without a concrete consumer use-case.\n\nProbe artifact: /tmp/pass29_probe2.py Q1 + Q2 / output at /tmp/pass29_output2.log. The matrix is reusable for future audits.\n\nNo status change. Pass-29 provides the structural enumeration for INV-virik's \"reserved provenance fields exist in the schema but are never populated\" face, generalized from per-field to per-(kind, field)."  # 7ccb
- op: discuss  # 0ab6
  at: '2026-06-02T08:02:26Z'  # 0ab6
  by: agent  # 0ab6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0ab6
  clock: 15  # 0ab6
  nonce: 0ab6  # 0ab6
  message: "Pass-32 face: `UsageContext` and `AnalysisRun` have `to_dict` but no `from_dict` — asymmetric serialization support (F32.8).\n\nINV-virik's scope: \"Reserved provenance fields exist in the schema but are never populated.\" Pass-32 surfaces a structurally adjacent face: **declared serializers exist in only one direction**. Specifically:\n\n- `Symbol`     has `to_dict` (ir.py:441) AND `from_dict` (ir.py:479) — symmetric\n- `Edge`       has `to_dict` (ir.py:714) AND `from_dict` (ir.py:762) — symmetric\n- `Span`       has `to_dict` (ir.py:147) AND `from_dict` (ir.py:156) — symmetric\n- `ExternalRef` has `to_dict` (ir.py:554) AND `from_dict` (ir.py:559) — symmetric\n- `UsageContext` has `to_dict` (ir.py:948) — **NO from_dict** (asymmetric)\n- `AnalysisRun`  has `to_dict` (ir.py:270) — **NO from_dict** (asymmetric)\n\nRound-trip empirical evidence (pass-32 probe C against `/tmp/p32_freshbm.json`):\n- Symbol: 34253/34253 round-trip byte-identically\n- Edge: 109915/109915 round-trip byte-identically\n- Span: 5000/5000 sampled spans round-trip byte-identically\n- Edge.edge_key: 109915/109915 recomputable from (src, dst, type) match substrate stored value\n- UsageContext: cannot round-trip — no `from_dict` (8 records in substrate)\n- AnalysisRun: cannot round-trip — no `from_dict` (84 records in substrate)\n\n**Why this fits INV-virik.** The original umbrella covers \"declared fields never populated\"; pass-32 generalizes to \"declared serialization-paths only in one direction.\" The schema-declaration-vs-actual-support pattern is the same: the writer's contract is fully implemented for the record class, but the reader's contract is partial. Consumers wanting to mutate-and-re-emit (a slice operation, a custom view, a synthetic test fixture) can do so for Symbol/Edge/Span/ExternalRef records but not for UsageContext or AnalysisRun records.\n\n**Concrete consequence.** Tools that need to programmatically generate a bm.json (e.g., test fixtures, synthetic substrate for fuzzing, fixture composers) must either (a) hand-build the AR/UC dicts directly without going through the dataclass, OR (b) work around the missing `from_dict` by reading raw and assuming structural correctness. Pass-32 itself ran into this when designing probe C: 4 record types could be tested via dataclass round-trip; 2 could only be observed via dict-level comparison.\n\n**Asymmetry detail.** AnalysisRun has 14 mutable fields (per pass-29 F29.1 schema-walk table). UsageContext has 8 keys per its substrate sample (`context_name, id, kind, metadata, path, position, span, symbol_ref`). Both are deterministic-enough at the substrate level that a `from_dict` is mechanically feasible; the asymmetry appears to be one of \"this class is consumer-only\" design rather than principled.\n\n**Related strong positive evidence (the round-trip NULL).** The full Symbol/Edge round-trip result — 34253 + 109915 records all byte-identical, 0 dropped fields, 0 added fields, 0 changed fields — is the strongest single piece of substrate-determinism evidence pass-32 produced. The writer-reader symmetry on the two highest-cardinality record types is bulletproof. This makes the UC/AR asymmetry stand out structurally: the **other** core record classes prove that symmetric serialization is achievable; UC/AR's missing `from_dict` is a real gap, not an architectural constraint.\n\n**No status change.** Pass-32 supplies a serialization-asymmetry face to INV-virik that generalizes the \"schema declares; producer doesn't populate\" pattern to \"class declares writer; class doesn't declare reader.\"\n\nProbe artifact: `/tmp/p32_outputC.log` (Symbol C.1, Edge C.2, UC C.3 — has no from_dict so the probe could only inspect dict shape, Span C.4, edge_key C.6)."  # 0ab6
