  nonce: '9902'  # 9902
  item: INV-virik-zobok-rakiv-lujop-budot-haduv-vimol-pigoj  # 9902
  target_nonce: 4f2a  # 9902
  new_text: "Pass-26 provenance-chain probes — reserved-empty / missing-field instances (F26.10 joint stable_id=None + language=None synthetic-kind cohort migrated to WI-libib-bapij per fold-audit Phase 2b; F26.9 and F26.14 retained as INV-virik extensions).\n\nF26.9: `bm.repo_fingerprint` is **None** at the top-level of bm.json, while `bm.repo_fingerprint_scheme` is populated (\"hypergumbo-repofp-v1\"). The scheme declaration implies the field exists in the schema. All 84 AR.repo_fingerprint values are identical (uniform `01531b2e29...`); the same fingerprint should be lifted to the bm-level field. Three options: (a) populate bm.repo_fingerprint from AR.repo_fingerprint (since they're uniform); (b) drop bm.repo_fingerprint from schema if AR-level is canonical; (c) document that bm.repo_fingerprint is intentionally absent (e.g., \"use ARs[0].repo_fingerprint\"). Status quo confuses consumers reading the top-level field.\n\nF26.14: `AR.warnings=[]` (empty list) on **all 84 ARs**. The field is declared in the AR dataclass (ir.py:200, `warnings: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)`) and serialized in every record. No AR ever writes anything to it. Pure reserved-empty extending the catalog already containing pass_version='' (14 ARs), partial_results_reason='' (top-level), origin_run_id='' (2228 nodes), failed_files=[] (limits + AR), etc.\n\nThe cumulative reserved-empty inventory across passes 23-26 (pass-23 F23.7 → WI-libib, pass-24 F24.2, pass-25 F25.4/F25.6, pass-26 F26.9/F26.14) and the F26.10 joint-NULL synthetic-kind cohort (now under WI-libib) are sibling faces of the same writer-conditional pattern. The \"schema field exists / writer never populates\" pattern that INV-virik umbrellas continues to surface at new fields each pass; the structural fix isn't piecewise — it's the kind-conditional / reason-conditional schema marking already discussed in WI-bujot's pass-25 thread and now consolidated under WI-libib's per-(kind,field) writer-contract validator scope."  # 9902
  reason: "fold-audit Phase 2b: F26.10 migrated to WI-libib; F26.9+F26.14 kept"  # 9902
